    },
    {
      "claim": "L5 verapamil-scaffold records show high intestinal permeability and near-complete absorption, with P-gp efflux present but not limiting absorption; this supports that the verapamil-like backbone can be absorbed.",
      "card_ids": ["C160", "C165", "C181", "C170", "C183", "C190", "C196"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "L5 also provides mechanistic evidence of intestinal CYP3A4/P-gp presystemic loss for verapamil, but no numeric absolute F is reported and the 'low oral bioavailability' statement in C171 is not quantified against the 20% threshold; mechanism alone is not a direct oral-bioavailability result.",
      "card_ids": ["C171", "C148", "C169", "C175", "C189"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "No L5 record tests the query's cyclic bis-sulfone modification, so transfer from verapamil is indirect and does not affirmatively establish F < 20%.",
      "card_ids": []
    }
  ],
  "new_evidence_assessment": [
    {
      "family": "gut_wall_efflux_intestinal_metabolism",
      "applicability": "moderate",
      "direction": "neutral_or_unclear",
      "decision_effect": "no_change",
      "card_ids": ["C171", "C148", "C169", "C175", "C189", "C160", "C165", "C181", "C170", "C183", "C190", "C196", "C179", "C193"]
    }
  ],
  "evidence_gaps": [
    "No query-specific absolute oral bioavailability or matched oral-versus-IV AUC/Cmax data are available.",
    "No query-specific pharmacokinetic data under cirrhosis are available; meptazinol is the only cirrhosis-matched L1 context.",
    "No query-specific gut-wall efflux or intestinal-metabolism data are available; L5 records are for verapamil and other molecules.",
    "No numeric F for verapamil is provided in L5; the 'low oral bioavailability' statement is not quantified against the 20% threshold.",
    "The effect of the query's cyclic bis-sulfone (1,3-dithiane tetraoxide) modification on permeability, P-gp efflux, and CYP3A4 metabolism is untested.",
    "Cirrhosis may alter first-pass metabolism, but the direction and magnitude for the query are unknown."
  ],
  "decision_summary": "Predicted high (F >= 20%) because the most direct cirrhosis-context gold record (meptazinol F 27.9%) and all other L1 gold contexts are at or above threshold; L5 verapamil-scaffold records show high intestinal absorption and efflux not limiting, while the intestinal CYP3A4/P-gp presystemic-loss evidence is mechanistic, unquantified, and not query-specific, so it does not affirmatively establish F < 20%. Confidence remains low due to absence of query-specific PK."
}

